---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { stats } from '../lib/data';
import { link } from '../lib/href';
const c = stats();
---
<Site active="about" title="About & provenance">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:1.4rem; max-width:760px;">
    <h1>About this reconstruction</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p><strong>kathakalinews.com</strong> — “A digital awakening in Kathakali” — was a hand-built community
      site that ran from roughly <strong>2008 to early 2014</strong>. It did two things: it hosted a reference
      library of Kathakali plays, ragas and the epics, and it ran a crowdsourced calendar where rasikas logged
      upcoming performances, archived quarterly.</p>
      <p>After it went dormant the domain was parked and later overrun by spam. This site is a faithful
      reconstruction built from the <strong>latest genuine snapshots in the Internet Archive</strong> (ignoring
      the later parking/spam captures).</p>
      <h3>What was recovered</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>{c.performances.toLocaleString()}</strong> performance records (2007–2011), parsed from 17 quarterly archive pages</li>
        <li><strong>{c.stories}</strong> attakatha (play) synopses with composers and vesham notes</li>
        <li><strong>{c.ragas}</strong> ragas with arohana / avarohana, janya and padam examples</li>
        <li>Ramayana / Mahabharata / Bhagavata summaries, the attams, and the Thodayam videos</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>How it's built</h3>
      <p>A fully <strong>static</strong> site generated with Astro. There is no database and no server: the source
      of truth is plain JSON in the repository, every page is rendered to flat HTML at build time, and the
      performance archive is searched entirely in your browser. The whole thing is a flat file set that can be
      hosted anywhere — or read offline from a folder. Everything is also published as <a href={link('/data')}>open data</a>.</p>
      <p class="muted">Reference content is indebted to K.P.S. Menon, the Kerala Sahitya Academy, and
      Prof. Aimanam Krishna Kaimal's <em>Kathakali Vijnana Kosham</em>. Original site by K. Srikumar / Shyam Srikumar.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Site>
